WEBVTT

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.950
<i>The drinking party for Accounting</i>
<i>last night saw sparks fly.</i>

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.910
<i>Now, another day begins at the office.</i>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.700
I am completely hungover.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:28.080
I don't even remember
how the party ended.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.040
<i>Wait... Didn't Retsuko...</i>

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.580
I'm pretty sure Retsuko
sang some sort of...

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:51.250
<i>Luckily, my inebriated co-workers</i>
<i>don't seem to clearly remember last night.</i>

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.450
<i>The only problem left...</i>

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.580
Good morning.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.620
I'm terribly sorry about last night!

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.620
Drunkenness is not an excuse
for being as rude as I was!

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.700
I don't remember...

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:22.160
I drank way too much last night.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:27.450
RAGE

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.000
KARAOKE

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:12.330
So you managed to retain your reputation
as a responsible good girl?

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.790
-It seems so.
-Well, that's boring.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.870
Oh, please! I much prefer it this way.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:22.870
By the way,

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.120
why is Director Gori frozen like that?

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.040
She's fine, don't worry.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.370
But...

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Let's not open that can of worms!

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.160
But she has turned into a statue!

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:38.000
Did something happen?

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.750
Heartbreak.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.120
But I still love him!

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.370
I know I was always
using my job as an excuse!

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.500
I also put up with a lot from him,
but I was so forgiving!

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.330
Maybe that is where I went wrong?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.660
Did I make him think
I would forgive anything?

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.580
I should have known that
we wouldn't understand each other.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.790
We live in two different worlds,
after all!

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.870
-Are you listening, Retsuko?
-Why did you follow me home?

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.660
I don't want to sleep on my own tonight.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.080
Just go back to your place already!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.330
You don't mind, do you? Besides,
I've always wanted to check out your room.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:29.450
-I'm borrowing this T-shirt.
-No!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.660
-Is there really nobody you like?
-No.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:39.200
-No nice suitors at work?
-Nobody!

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.370
You don't want to spill the beans.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.700
But it's nice to dream about it. Right?

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:51.250
Your soulmate could be
somewhere in this city.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.370
Oh, my...

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.540
Resasuke, this is problematic.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:08.790
How many times have I told you
that we don't accept illegible receipts?

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.120
I'm sorry.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.870
Let me guess. You put it
in your back pocket and forgot about it?

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:15.790
Yes.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.250
-And then you put it through the wash?
-Yes.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.370
That's another expense
you have to cover yourself.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.450
The Out-of-Pocket Prince.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.040
-The Out-of-Pocket Prince?
-The spaced-out guy from Sales.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.330
-He always gets in trouble.
-I don't know him.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.870
Yes, he's not exactly memorable.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:49.910
Ms. Retsuko!

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:51.660
Hi, Tsunoda.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.910
Thank you for taking me out to dinner
the other night.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.290
Hello to you too, Ms. Fenneko.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.160
I know this is abrupt...

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.660
-Is there someone you like?
-Huh?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.580
No, there isn't...

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.950
Then would you join our singles mixer?

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.500
A mixer?

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.120
No... I'm not into that kind of thing.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.200
I know that you want a boyfriend.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:20.290
You should come.
This is your chance to meet some guys.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.830
Come on, join us!

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.410
Tsunoda, Retsuko isn't interested.
Cut it out.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.040
-Why?
-Mixers are on the way out.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.540
A study in Japan has shown that 75% of men

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.450
and 65% of women
in their 20s and 30s have no partner.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.370
In other words, more and more people

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:45.290
are choosing the more economical option
of single life!

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:49.500
-With that in mind, do you want to join?
-What?

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:52.700
What do you mean, "With that in mind"?
Did you hear what I said?

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.830
I did, but I didn't understand.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:59.870
Fenneko said that she's coming,
so you should come as well!

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.540
I never said that!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.500
A mixer? Sounds good.

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:11.620
I'm not used to such activities...

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.040
Your soulmate might be there!

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.330
My soulmate?

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.250
I don't fall in love that easily.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:29.410
Retsuko, stop doubting yourself
and put yourself out there.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.660
In the right circumstances...

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.410
...anyone can fall in love...

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.620
...instantly!

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:44.580
Why did you give into
this mixer thing so easily?

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:46.750
I don't know!

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.450
I underestimated her.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.660
I didn't realize Tsunoda was so good
at dragging people into her schemes.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.700
-But don't worry. I'll protect her.
-What?

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:04.160
I'll do my best to protect Retsuko
from those bloodthirsty guys.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.620
So you'll go as her bodyguard?

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:11.290
Please, Fenneko!
You are my only hope.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.370
Leave it to me.

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:40.500
<i>The Out-of-Pocket Prince!</i>

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:42.750
<i>He travels on the same train.</i>

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:45.870
<i>I didn't have a clue.</i>

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:51.540
<i>Maybe I should say hi</i>
<i>when we get off the train.</i>

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:55.250
<i>Wait, how would that</i>
<i>amount to anything?</i>

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.750
<i>We'd end up quietly walking to work,</i>
<i>but not quite together.</i>

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.370
<i>Anyway, he doesn't even know me.</i>

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.410
<i>What a pain.</i>
<i>I wish I hadn't noticed him.</i>

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:23.410
<i>Wait… The office...</i>

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.200
<i>What a weirdo.</i>

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:38.700
There are two escape routes:
the main entrance and the emergency exit.

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:41.160
If you get in trouble,
the police station is opposite.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.750
-Got it?
-Yeah.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:47.540
Ms. Fenneko, please, just chill out.

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.790
I'm not here to relax, you know!

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:52.950
Retsuko, I'll protect you
if some freak sets his sights on you.

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:56.500
No freaks are coming tonight.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:58.750
How can you be so sure?

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:02.160
Because all of them
are from the Sales department.

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.370
-From the office?
-That's right.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.950
Didn't I mention it was a company mixer?

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.250
-Company...
-Mixer?

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:17.870
-Hi, I'm Manumaru!
-Hello. I'm Rinta.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.870
Say hello!

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:27.330
The Out-of-Pocket Prince.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.620
-What?
-Nothing.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.750
This guy here is Resasuke.

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:36.500
He came to even out the numbers,
so don't mind him.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:39.120
Don't you think
that's a mean thing to say?

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:45.080
I am Retsuko from Accounting.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:50.120
-Nice to meet you. You're cute!
-What?

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:52.700
You remind me of someone...

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:56.450
Has anyone ever said
you resemble a Sanrio character?

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.290
On occasion...

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:05.410
-Who is this, Tsunoda?
-Fenneko, from Accounting.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.290
Nice to meet you. You're cute, too!

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.830
<i>Mixers aren't that bad after all...</i>

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:21.700
-Oh, that's easy-peasy!
-Seriously?

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:24.330
-To put it another way...
-Where did you hear that?

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:32.040
<i>I missed my chance</i>
<i>to join the conversation...</i>

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.250
<i>not that I really mind.</i>

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.500
<i>I don't want to look bored, though.</i>

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.870
<i>What can we talk about?</i>

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:48.500
Hi, I saw you on the train yesterday.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.580
Do you always use the Den-en-toshi line?

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:56.290
You didn't get off at the station
closest to work.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.160
What happened after that?

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:05.660
Well...

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.700
You must be joking, buddy.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.660
<i>You're a riot!</i>

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.790
<i>Did he say something?</i>

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:21.700
<i>He is so quiet.</i>

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.370
Sorry. It's a little noisy...

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.290
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:43.120
ADD FRIEND

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.080
RESASUKE

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:45.080
ADD

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.580
CONCERNING THE TRAIN...

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:57.000
I ARRIVED LATE.

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:59.450
SEND

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:07.250
<i>Concerning the train, I was daydreaming.</i>
<i>I missed my stop and arrived late.</i>

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:16.290
<i>May I ask you something?</i>

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:17.910
<i>Of course.</i>

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:20.450
<i>Why are you drinking coffee in a can?</i>

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.620
<i>I'm not fond of alcohol.</i>

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.370
<i>I understand, but why coffee in a can?</i>

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:39.700
-Haida! Hey, Haida!
<i>-Don't shout. I can hear you.</i>

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:43.500
Mixers are a lot more fun than I thought.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:45.660
<i>I don't give a damn about that!</i>

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:48.950
-How is Retsuko?
<i>-She's fine. No need to worry.</i>

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.250
She isn't cut out for this scene.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.620
She spent the entire party
tapping away at her phone.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:55.910
<i>I see.</i>

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:01.040
Anyway, Haida, you're a wimp.
Go and ask her out already, you idiot!

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:05.330
<i>I'm not cut out for partying.</i>

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.450
<i>Neither am I.</i>

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:14.830
<i>Somehow, I feel really relaxed.</i>

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:20.330
<i>There is a certain stillness</i>
<i>enveloping us.</i>

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.700
COFFEE

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:27.410
<i>Huh?</i>

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.870
<i>I might be getting drunk...</i>

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.410
Hello?

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.790
Retsuko?

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:47.160
-Retsuko!
-Retsuko, are you OK?

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:52.040
<i>Strange...</i>
<i>When did I manage to drink so much?</i>

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.120
RESTROOM

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:16.870
Are you OK?

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:23.500
Thank you.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:29.830
<i>In the right circumstances...</i>

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.160
<i>...anyone can fall in love...</i>

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:34.790
<i>...instantly!</i>

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:10.910
Subtitle translation: John Haguewood
